<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  ============================================================================
  SURFACE A — THE GATE.  14-auth.md §5.
  ============================================================================

  ONE BLOCK, NOT TWO ANCHORS.  Owner test 2026-07-27, item C3: «когда нажимаешь
  войти, надо чтобы кнопки были выше». The first build of this screen pinned the
  intro to the top and the actions to the bottom, and on a 6.7-inch phone that
  left a headline stranded above 300dp of nothing with two buttons parked on the
  bezel. It reads as a screen that failed to load, not as a composition.

  So the heading, the sub-line and the actions are now ONE group — 32dp apart,
  read as a unit — floated by a pair of weighted spacers, 3 above and 4 below.
  The 3:4 split puts the group a touch above the optical centre, which is where
  the eye lands and where the thumb already is; nothing sits on the bottom edge
  and nothing is stranded at the top.

  The spacers are still the composition and not left-over room: fillViewport +
  weight means a short viewport (landscape, split screen, font scale 200%)
  collapses both to nothing and the whole column scrolls. Nothing is ever
  clipped and nothing overlaps.

  THE FLOORS ARE THE COLUMN'S PADDING, NOT minHeight ON THE SPACERS. A weighted
  child is re-measured with an EXACTLY spec, and Space.onMeasure returns the spec
  size verbatim under EXACTLY — its minHeight is discarded. Written that way the
  floors silently were not there, and at font scale 200% the heading sat flush
  against the toolbar with the last button flush against the gesture bar. The
  24/32 live on the column instead, where LinearLayout subtracts them before it
  distributes the weights, so they hold in both directions.

  ONE FILLED ACCENT SURFACE, and it is @id/btn_gate_telegram. The Telegram glyph
  is tinted colorOnPrimary, NEVER Telegram's own blue — a second brand hue on the
  product's one accent is banned (00-rules.md 1.4.1).

  ZERO CARDS. 03-direction.md 10.1: the sign-in form is not an object floating on
  a surface, it is the screen.

  THE WAIT IS A LEDGER ROW (5.3). 40dp leading slot, 12dp gap, text origin 68dp —
  identical to every list row in the app, so the most unusual moment in the
  product is built from its most ordinary part. That is why the awaiting state is
  not a centred hero spinner with a paragraph under it.

  THE ACTION SLOT NEVER CHANGES HEIGHT. The awaiting stack is 64dp taller than
  the idle one, and while it was GONE that difference moved the whole column the
  instant the crossfade started — a layout jump under a 200ms fade, which is the
  cheapest-looking thing a transition can do. It is INVISIBLE instead, so the
  FrameLayout is always measured against the taller of the two and the heading,
  the CTA and the row that replaces it all sit on exactly the same baseline. An
  invisible view is out of the accessibility tree and its progress indicator
  stops animating, so nothing is paid for the stability.

  THE ERROR LINE SITS ABOVE THE ACTION SLOT: it belongs to the intro's half of
  the group, so a two-line failure grows upwards into the lead spacer instead of
  shoving the buttons down under the thumb. Start-aligned at the gutter, like
  every other line here; the old centred grey-red line at the bottom of a scroll
  is deleted.
-->
<androidx.core.widget.NestedScrollView xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    xmlns:app="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res-auto"
    xmlns:tools="http://schemas.android.com/tools"
    android:id="@+id/gate_scroll"
    android:layout_width="match_parent"
    android:layout_height="match_parent"
    android:clipToPadding="false"
    android:fillViewport="true"
    android:paddingStart="@dimen/screen_gutter"
    android:paddingEnd="@dimen/screen_gutter"
    android:scrollbars="none">

    <LinearLayout
        android:layout_width="match_parent"
        android:layout_height="wrap_content"
        android:orientation="vertical"
        android:paddingTop="@dimen/space_24"
        android:paddingBottom="@dimen/space_32">

        <!-- The lead spacer. Weight 3 against the trail's 4, so the group settles
             just above the optical centre instead of on the top edge. It carries
             no minHeight: an EXACTLY spec ignores one, and the floor above it is
             the column's own padding. -->
        <Space
            android:id="@+id/gate_lead"
            android:layout_width="match_parent"
            android:layout_height="0dp"
            android:layout_weight="3" />

        <LinearLayout
            android:id="@+id/gate_intro"
            android:layout_width="match_parent"
            android:layout_height="wrap_content"
            android:orientation="vertical">

            <!-- «Вход в departament». The Latin token is re-set in the brand face
                 at bind time (D-14.1); that span is the whole brand moment on this
                 screen and is why there is no logo, no shield tile and no wordmark
                 lockup above it. -->
            <TextView
                android:id="@+id/gate_title"
                android:layout_width="match_parent"
                android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                android:accessibilityHeading="true"
                android:maxLines="2"
                android:text="@string/auth_gate_title"
                android:textAppearance="@style/TextAppearance.App.Headline"
                android:textColor="?attr/colorOnSurface" />

            <TextView
                android:id="@+id/gate_body"
                android:layout_width="match_parent"
                android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                android:layout_marginTop="@dimen/space_8"
                android:maxLines="3"
                android:text="@string/auth_gate_body"
                android:textAppearance="@style/TextAppearance.App.Body"
                android:textColor="?attr/colorOnSurfaceVariant" />
        </LinearLayout>

        <!-- 32dp, the same step that separates a section from its content
             everywhere else, is what ties the heading to what it is asking for.
             It is a margin and not a spacer: this gap never stretches. -->
        <LinearLayout
            android:id="@+id/gate_actions"
            android:layout_width="match_parent"
            android:layout_height="wrap_content"
            android:layout_marginTop="@dimen/space_32"
            android:orientation="vertical">

            <!-- Screen-level error: Body 14/400 in the error TEXT red (6.15:1),
                 not the 4.88:1 fill red. Field errors are Caption 12 (D-14.3). -->
            <TextView
                android:id="@+id/gate_error"
                android:layout_width="match_parent"
                android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                android:layout_marginBottom="@dimen/space_12"
                android:accessibilityLiveRegion="polite"
                android:textAppearance="@style/TextAppearance.App.Body"
                android:textColor="@color/color_destructive_text"
                android:visibility="gone"
                tools:text="@string/auth_err_network"
                tools:visibility="visible" />

            <!-- The crossfade host: exactly one stack is READABLE at a time, but
                 both are always MEASURED, so the slot is the taller one's height
                 in every state and nothing below the heading ever moves. -->
            <FrameLayout
                android:id="@+id/gate_action_slot"
                android:layout_width="match_parent"
                android:layout_height="wrap_content">

                <LinearLayout
                    android:id="@+id/gate_stack_idle"
                    android:layout_width="match_parent"
                    android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                    android:orientation="vertical">

                    <!-- The button and its loading arc share a frame so R8 can hide
                         the label without the control changing width: the button is
                         match_parent, so the width is pinned by the layout itself. -->
                    <FrameLayout
                        android:layout_width="match_parent"
                        android:layout_height="wrap_content">

                        <com.google.android.material.button.MaterialButton
                            android:id="@+id/btn_gate_telegram"
                            style="@style/Widget.Departament.Button.Primary.Tall"
                            android:layout_width="match_parent"
                            android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                            android:text="@string/auth_btn_telegram"
                            app:icon="@drawable/ic_telegram_24dp" />

                        <com.google.android.material.progressindicator.CircularProgressIndicator
                            android:id="@+id/pb_gate_telegram"
                            style="@style/Widget.Departament.Progress.Circular.Inline.OnAccent"
                            android:layout_width="wrap_content"
                            android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                            android:layout_gravity="center"
                            android:visibility="gone"
                            tools:visibility="visible" />
                    </FrameLayout>

                    <com.google.android.material.button.MaterialButton
                        android:id="@+id/btn_gate_email"
                        style="@style/Widget.Departament.Button.Tertiary"
                        android:layout_width="match_parent"
                        android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                        android:layout_marginTop="@dimen/space_12"
                        android:text="@string/auth_btn_email" />
                </LinearLayout>

                <LinearLayout
                    android:id="@+id/gate_stack_awaiting"
                    android:layout_width="match_parent"
                    android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                    android:orientation="vertical"
                    android:visibility="invisible"
                    tools:visibility="visible">

                    <!-- The universal 56dp row: 40 slot, 12 gap, text at 68 from the
                         screen edge (16 gutter on the scroll + 40 + 12). Read as one
                         node by TalkBack and announced politely when it appears. -->
                    <LinearLayout
                        android:id="@+id/gate_awaiting_row"
                        android:layout_width="match_parent"
                        android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                        android:accessibilityLiveRegion="polite"
                        android:baselineAligned="false"
                        android:gravity="center_vertical"
                        android:minHeight="@dimen/row_min_height"
                        android:orientation="horizontal">

                        <FrameLayout
                            android:id="@+id/gate_ring"
                            android:layout_width="@dimen/tile_size"
                            android:layout_height="@dimen/tile_size">

                            <com.google.android.material.progressindicator.CircularProgressIndicator
                                android:id="@+id/gate_ring_arc"
                                style="@style/Widget.Departament.Progress.Circular.Inline"
                                android:layout_width="@dimen/tile_size"
                                android:layout_height="@dimen/tile_size"
                                app:indicatorSize="@dimen/tile_size"
                                app:trackColor="?attr/colorOutlineVariant" />

                            <!-- The success beat's terminal frame: the arc fades out,
                                 the check fades and scales in, 120ms hold, done. -->
                            <ImageView
                                android:id="@+id/gate_ring_check"
                                android:layout_width="@dimen/glyph_20"
                                android:layout_height="@dimen/glyph_20"
                                android:layout_gravity="center"
                                android:alpha="0"
                                android:importantForAccessibility="no"
                                android:src="@drawable/ic_fab_check"
                                app:tint="?attr/colorPrimary" />
                        </FrameLayout>

                        <LinearLayout
                            android:layout_width="0dp"
                            android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                            android:layout_marginStart="@dimen/space_12"
                            android:layout_weight="1"
                            android:orientation="vertical">

                            <TextView
                                android:id="@+id/gate_awaiting_title"
                                android:layout_width="match_parent"
                                android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                                android:maxLines="2"
                                android:text="@string/auth_awaiting_title"
                                android:textAppearance="@style/TextAppearance.App.Title"
                                android:textColor="?attr/colorOnSurface" />

                            <TextView
                                android:id="@+id/gate_awaiting_body"
                                android:layout_width="match_parent"
                                android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                                android:layout_marginTop="@dimen/space_4"
                                android:maxLines="2"
                                android:text="@string/auth_awaiting_body"
                                android:textAppearance="@style/TextAppearance.App.Subtitle"
                                android:textColor="?attr/colorOnSurfaceVariant" />
                        </LinearLayout>
                    </LinearLayout>

                    <!-- Two tertiaries is the cap (R14.6) and this stack is exactly
                         at it. There is no «Начать заново»: restarting is what the
                         primary CTA does, and the timeout state puts that CTA back
                         on screen by itself. Cancel is system Back. -->
                    <com.google.android.material.button.MaterialButton
                        android:id="@+id/btn_gate_open_telegram"
                        style="@style/Widget.Departament.Button.Tertiary"
                        android:layout_width="match_parent"
                        android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                        android:layout_marginTop="@dimen/space_12"
                        android:text="@string/auth_open_telegram" />

                    <com.google.android.material.button.MaterialButton
                        android:id="@+id/btn_gate_email_alt"
                        style="@style/Widget.Departament.Button.Tertiary"
                        android:layout_width="match_parent"
                        android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                        android:layout_marginTop="@dimen/space_12"
                        android:text="@string/auth_btn_email" />
                </LinearLayout>
            </FrameLayout>
        </LinearLayout>

        <!-- The trail spacer. Weight 4 against the lead's 3: it keeps the group
             off the bottom edge and off the gesture bar, and it is the one that
             gives way first when the viewport gets short. Same as the lead — the
             floor below it is the column's padding, not a minHeight. -->
        <Space
            android:id="@+id/gate_spacer"
            android:layout_width="match_parent"
            android:layout_height="0dp"
            android:layout_weight="4" />
    </LinearLayout>
</androidx.core.widget.NestedScrollView>
